  "term": "waxy flexibility",
  "definition": "Waxy flexibility is a state in which a person shows very little movement or response and keeps an unmoving posture, with the limbs staying in whatever position they are placed. It is described as a feature of catalepsy and can occur in psychotic disorders, drug toxicity affecting the nervous system, and other conditions.",
